---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Jorge Liauw Calo | Security Engineer at Google Cloud"
  description="Learn more about Jorge Liauw Calo — Security Engineer at Google Cloud with 13+ years of experience in Cybersecurity across Semiconductor, Banking, Fintech, and Insurance."
  image="/images/jorge-nike-running-shoes-miami-harbor.webp"
>
  <section class="py-14 lg:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <!-- Hero Intro -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center mb-16">
        <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-5">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-400 block">About Me</span>
          <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
            Security Engineer at Google Cloud &amp; Cybersecurity Specialist
          </h1>
          <p class="text-lg text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
            I currently work at <strong class="text-white font-semibold">Google Cloud as a Security Engineer</strong> and am part of the <strong class="text-emerald-400 font-semibold">Google Cybershield team</strong>. With <strong class="text-white font-semibold">13+ years of experience in Cybersecurity</strong>, I have consistently worked with customers in high-security and highly regulated industries including <strong class="text-cyan-400">Semiconductor, Banking, Fintech, and Insurance</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-base text-slate-400 leading-relaxed">
            I am an active member of the <strong class="text-slate-200">Google Cloud Community BeNeLux</strong> and <strong class="text-slate-200">Google Cloud Security Community Amsterdam</strong>, bringing cloud security practitioners and engineers together to share knowledge, architectures, and security best practices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-4">
          <div class="relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 shadow-2xl bg-slate-900">
            <img
              src="/images/jorge-google-cloud-2.jpg"
              alt="Jorge Liauw Calo at Google Bay View campus"
              class="w-full h-64 sm:h-72 object-cover object-center"
            />
            <div class="p-3.5 bg-slate-900/95 border-t border-slate-800 text-center">
              <p class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-400">
                At Google Bay View Campus &bull; Mountain View, CA
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="relative rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 shadow-xl bg-slate-900 flex items-center gap-4 p-3">
            <img
              src="/images/jorge-running.webp"
              alt="Jorge Liauw Calo running"
              class="w-16 h-16 rounded-xl object-cover shrink-0 border border-slate-700"
            />
            <p class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              &ldquo;Hi! I'm Jorge — a passionate runner who loves Google Cloud and Cybersecurity.&rdquo;
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Career Journey Timeline -->
      <div class="mb-20">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-end justify-between mb-8 gap-4">
          <div>
            <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-400 block mb-1">Experience &amp; Roles</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
              To the Cloud and Beyond — Career Timeline
            </h2>
          </div>
          <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/jorgeliauw/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-400 hover:text-cyan-300"
          >
            <span>View full LinkedIn profile</span>
            <span>&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6 relative before:absolute before:top-4 before:bottom-4 before:left-4 sm:before:left-6 before:w-0.5 before:bg-slate-800">
          <!-- Google Cloud (Current) -->
          <div class="relative pl-12 sm:pl-16">
            <span class="absolute left-2.5 sm:left-4.5 top-1.5 w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-400 ring-4 ring-slate-950 animate-pulse"></span>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/90 border border-emerald-500/40 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/5">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Security Engineer &bull; Google Cloud</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Amsterdam, Netherlands</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-400 border border-emerald-500/30 font-semibold">Present</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                Working at <strong class="text-white">Google Cloud</strong> as a Security Engineer (Customer Engineer Security) and part of the <strong class="text-emerald-400">Google Cybershield team</strong>, partnering with enterprise customers in high-security and highly regulated industries—such as <strong class="text-white">Semiconductor, Banking, Fintech, and Insurance</strong>—to secure mission-critical cloud workloads, infrastructure, and data. Active contributor to the <strong class="text-white">Google Cloud Community BeNeLux</strong> and <strong class="text-white">Google Cloud Security Community Amsterdam</strong>.
              </p>
              <div class="mt-3 pt-3 border-t border-slate-800/80 flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono text-cyan-300">
                <span>Mission:</span>
                <span class="italic text-slate-200">&ldquo;Our goal is bigger than securing Google — it’s about securing the internet.&rdquo;</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Xebia (Past Experience) -->
          <div class="relative pl-12 sm:pl-16">
            <span class="absolute left-2.5 sm:left-4.5 top-1.5 w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-cyan-400 ring-4 ring-slate-950"></span>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Google Cloud Security Architect &bull; Xebia</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Binx.io / Xebia Cloud</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-800 text-slate-300">Feb 2022 &ndash; 2024</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                With more than 12 years of experience in IT, Cloud, and Cybersecurity at the time, I worked as a Google Cloud Security Architect at <a href="https://xebia.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Xebia</a>, helping organizations take their cloud security to the next level.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                Since joining Xebia in February 2022, I had the honor of working with industry-leading customers like <strong class="text-white">Mollie</strong> and <strong class="text-white">ASML</strong> to design resilient Google Cloud security architectures. Beyond client engagements, I frequently gave talks, workshops, and trainings on Google Cloud Security, co-organized the <strong class="text-white">Google Cloud User Group Benelux</strong>, and was awarded the <strong class="text-amber-400">Google Cloud Partner All-Star (2022)</strong> for Excellence in Solutions Engineering &amp; Delivery.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Freelance & PwC -->
          <div class="relative pl-12 sm:pl-16">
            <span class="absolute left-2.5 sm:left-4.5 top-1.5 w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-blue-400 ring-4 ring-slate-950"></span>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Independent Cybersecurity &amp; Cloud Consultant &bull; PwC / Freelance</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Financial Services &amp; Enterprise Security</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-800 text-slate-300">2018 &ndash; Feb 2022</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                Worked for four years as an independent Cybersecurity &amp; Cloud consultant, including serving as a Cybersecurity Consultant at <strong class="text-white">PwC</strong> (2018). Delivered high-impact security projects, cloud security assessments, and architecture advisory for major financial institutions including <strong class="text-white">ING</strong> and <strong class="text-white">ABN AMRO Clearing Bank</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Deviate Private Cloud -->
          <div class="relative pl-12 sm:pl-16">
            <span class="absolute left-2.5 sm:left-4.5 top-1.5 w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-purple-400 ring-4 ring-slate-950"></span>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Cloud Pioneer &amp; Co-Founder &bull; Deviate</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Private Cloud &amp; High Availability Infrastructure</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-800 text-slate-300">2014 &ndash; 2018</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                Ran our own early version of what would become modern Cloud infrastructure. At Deviate, we operated multiple servers across two datacenters connected via a secure interconnect with a hypervisor layer capable of automated Virtual Machine failover between datacenters—delivering non-stop high availability for mobile application workloads.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Information Analyst & TIBCO -->
          <div class="relative pl-12 sm:pl-16">
            <span class="absolute left-2.5 sm:left-4.5 top-1.5 w-3.5 h-3.5 rounded-full bg-slate-500 ring-4 ring-slate-950"></span>
            <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2 mb-2">
                <div>
                  <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Information Analyst &amp; TIBCO Integration Consultant</h3>
                  <span class="text-xs font-mono text-slate-400">Banking, Insurance &amp; Enterprise Integration</span>
                </div>
                <span class="text-xs font-mono px-2.5 py-1 rounded bg-slate-800 text-slate-300">2011 &ndash; 2014</span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mt-2">
                Started my career after graduating in 2011 as an Information Analyst and TIBCO Integration Consultant. Designed and implemented mission-critical IT solutions for large banks, insurance companies, and pension funds (Clearing &amp; Settlement), and built enterprise workflows in TIBCO ActiveMatrix BusinessWorks (AMX) and TIBCO BPM for <strong class="text-white">NN</strong>, <strong class="text-white">ING</strong>, and <strong class="text-white">Van Gansewinkel</strong>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- How It All Started Section -->
      <div class="p-8 sm:p-10 rounded-3xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800/90">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center">
          <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-4">
            <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-400 block">Origins</span>
            <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
              How It All Started: From COAX Rings to Healthcare IT
            </h2>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              At age 11, I worked for the first time on a computer with an internet connection at my high school—an old PC running <strong class="text-white">Windows 95</strong>. The computers were linked via a <strong class="text-white">COAX ring network</strong> sharing a 128 kbit/s ISDN dial-up line (bundling two 64 kbit/s channels) across more than 10 workstations.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              I was given the opportunity to help transition the school to a modern network based on Ethernet switches, high-speed broadband, and Windows 2000 Pro workstations connected to an Active Directory domain controller enforcing Group Policies.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              My fascination began with the <strong class="text-white">Apple Macintosh 128K</strong>, while my earliest gaming and coding memories were on an <strong class="text-white">Atari 2600</strong>, <strong class="text-white">Commodore 64</strong>, and a <strong class="text-white">386 MS-DOS PC</strong> with a green monochrome monitor at age 10—inspired by my grandfather (who worked for the SWIFT financial network), my brother, and my cousin.
            </p>
            <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              By age 16, I started my own IT business designing reliable servers and networks for doctors and dentists. My biggest driver was engineering dependable, secure systems that directly protected patients—for example, ensuring a failing IT system never forced a patient to undergo a repeat X-ray exposure. <strong class="text-cyan-300">Technology should always make life better, faster, and safer!</strong>
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="lg:col-span-4">
            <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 p-3 shadow-xl">
              <img
                src="/images/Apple-Macintosh-128K.webp"
                alt="Apple Macintosh 128K"
                class="w-full rounded-xl object-cover"
              />
              <p class="text-xs text-center text-slate-400 font-mono mt-3">
                The Apple Macintosh 128K that sparked a lifelong passion for computing.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
